39533408 17592186045585 false] [17592186097199 1068 #edb/ref 17592186095122 13194139533408 17592186045585 false] [17592186097199 1068 #edb/ref 17592186289824 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186097199 1068 #edb/ref 17592186289989 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186097199 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186097199 1071 "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{5}{2}a+3b=-6 \\\\ \\frac{5}{3}a-\\frac{1}{3}b=9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$a=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,b=$\n{{field-2}}" 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186097199 1071 "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n${-\\frac{5}{2}a + 3b =-6; \\frac{5}{3}a - \\frac{1}{3}b = 9$\n\n$a =$\n{{field-1}} $, b =$\n{{field-2}}" 13194139533408 17592186045585 false] [17592186097199 1074 "To get rid of fractions, we multiply the first equation by $2$ and the second equation by $3,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{5}{2}a+3b=-6 & |\\times 2 \\\\ \\frac{5}{3}a-\\frac{1}{3}b=9 & |\\times 3\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}-5a+6b=-12 \\\\ 5a-b=27\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will use the elimination method to solve the system. We can eliminate $a$ by adding the two equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\cancel{5a}+6b & =-12 \\\\ \\cancel{5a}-b & =27 \\\\ (6b-b) & =(-12+27) \\\\ 5b & =15 \\\\ b & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $b=3$ into the second equation to solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5a-b & =27 \\\\ 5a-3 & =27 \\\\ 5a & =30 \\\\ a & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system is $a=6,\\,b=3.$" 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186097207 1068 #edb/ref 17592186095141 13194139533408 17592186045585 false] [17592186097207 1068 #edb/ref 17592186289859 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186097207 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186097207 1071 "Find $y^{′}$ for $y = (\\tan (7x - 2))/(4x)$." 13194139533408 17592186045585 false] [17592186097207 1071 "Find ${y}^{′}$ for $y=\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡(7x-2)}{4x}.$" 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186097207 1074 "We use the quotient rule with the numerator $u(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(7x-2)$ and the denominator $v(x)=4x.$ \n\nDifferentiating $u(x)$ and $v(x),$ we have\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}(x)=7{sec}^{2}⁡(7x-2),\\,{v}^{′}(x)=4.\n$$\n\nNote that we used the chain rule to differentiate $u.$\n\nNow, applying the quotient rule and simplifying, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(7{sec}^{2}⁡(7x-2))(4x)-\\operatorname{tan}⁡(7x-2)(4)}{(4x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4(7x{sec}^{2}⁡(7x-2)-\\operatorname{tan}⁡(7x-2))}{16{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{⧸}4(7x{sec}^{2}⁡(7x-2)-\\operatorname{tan}⁡(7x-2))}{\\text{⧸}4(4{x}^{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{7x{sec}^{2}⁡(7x-2)-\\operatorname{tan}⁡(7x-2)}{4{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186100819 1038 #edb/ref 17592186290284 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186100819 1038 #edb/ref 17592186290285 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186100820 1038 #edb/ref 17592186290286 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186100822 1038 #edb/ref 17592186290281 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186100822 1038 #edb/ref 17592186290282 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186100822 1038 #edb/ref 17592186290514 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186100823 1038 #edb/ref 17592186290283 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186100823 1038 #edb/ref 17592186290287 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186100875 1038 #edb/ref 17592186290375 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186100875 1038 #edb/ref 17592186290376 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186100875 1038 #edb/ref 17592186290377 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186100896 1038 #edb/ref 17592186290553 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186100896 1038 #edb/r