 \\cdot \\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta }{{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta }\n$$\n\nWe now simplify the expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta }{{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta } & =\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\cancel{\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta }}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we recall the following identities:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta },\\,\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta }=\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\n \n\nUsing the above identities, we can further simplify our expression as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta } & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }}\\cdot \\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta }{1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta }=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$" 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186115363 1038 #edb/ref 17592186290619 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186115363 1038 #edb/ref 17592186290620 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186115363 1038 #edb/ref 17592186290621 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186115363 1038 #edb/ref 17592186290622 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186115364 1038 #edb/ref 17592186290623 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17