045585 true] [17592186290619 1071 "![](images/fb/fbccea4652fde939777bd69f621497f9e63ee79c7d4e4f0a5327bb141ce021ca.png)\n\nIn square units rounded to the nearest integer, the area of $△ABC$ is{{field-1}}." 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290619 1072 #uuid "6710d2e0-8c0d-5c72-9f96-112ffd2507b9" 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290619 1074 "In this case, the area of a right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nNotice that relative to the given angle $∠B,$ we have the length of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{AC}$ and need to determine the length of the adjacent side $\\overset{―}{BC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $BC:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠B) & =\\frac{AC}{BC} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡({70}^{∘}) & =\\frac{6}{BC} \\\\ BC\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡({70}^{∘}) & =6 \\\\ BC & =\\frac{6}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡({70}^{∘})} \\\\ BC & =2.183…\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 6\\cdot (2.183…) \\\\  & =6.551… \\\\  & ≈7,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer." 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290620 1068 #edb/ref 17592186289968 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290620 1069 "q-251069" 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290620 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290620 1071 "![](images/85/85344df61b503271cd23cb3c741cd659b1417cb34b9031f0283dcf9c8fae6794.png)\n\nIn square units rounded to the nearest integer, the area of $△ABC$ is{{field-1}}." 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290620 1072 #uuid "5ce2689f-7fa1-5f63-bd2a-e8d763190131" 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290620 1074 "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nNotice that relative to the given angle $∠B,$ we have the length of the adjacent side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ and need to determine the length of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{AC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $AC:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠B) & =\\frac{AC}{BC} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡({20}^{∘}) & =\\frac{AC}{12} \\\\ AC & =12\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡({20}^{∘}) \\\\ AC & =4.367…\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (4.367…)\\cdot 12 \\\\  & =26.205… \\\\  & ≈26,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer." 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290621 1068 #edb/ref 17592186289856 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290621 1069 "q-251070" 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290621 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290621 1071 "![](images/ed/ed3de6f6fe96fab30d6f3927582a00ee9d0edc1f2514fec17507e2398009217f.png)\n\nIn square units rounded to the nearest integer, the area of $△ABC$ is{{field-1}}." 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290621 1072 #uuid "994386cd-5246-55a1-9563-16d2ef819cb7" 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290621 1074 "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nNotice that relative to the given angle $∠B,$ we have the length of the adjacent side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ and need to determine the length of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{AC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $AC:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠B) & =\\frac{AC}{BC} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡({30}^{∘}) & =\\frac{AC}{5} \\\\ AC & =5\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡({30}^{∘}) \\\\ AC & =2.886…\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (2.886…)\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =7.216… \\\\  & ≈7,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer." 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290622 1068 #edb/ref 17592186290083 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290622 1069 "q-251074" 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290622 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290622 1071 "![](images/e7/e72091463bf8f973629ff1467ae8ca184689b4745c387acac618b8a81876c52f.png)\n\nIn square units rounded to the nearest integer, the area of $△ABC$ is{{field-1}}." 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290622 1072 #uuid "db45a1cb-4670-5290-9912-a48f4d70e058" 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290622 1074 "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nNotice that relative to the given angle $∠B,$ we have the length of the adjacent side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ and need to determine the length of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{AC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $AC:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠B) & =\\frac{AC}{BC} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡({28}^{∘}) & =\\frac{AC}{14} \\\\ AC & =14\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡({28}^{∘}) \\\\ AC & =7.443…\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (7.443…)\\cdot 14 \\\\  & =52.107… \\\\  & ≈52,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer." 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290623 1068 #edb/ref 17592186290200 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290623 1069 "q-251078" 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290623 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290623 1071 "![](images/7a/7acf00fc8ac1ac67612b740450fe62f7cddee2a9fc7a9c28fe54fafb2c1ee57c.png)\n\nGiven that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠B)=\\frac{5}{2},$ the **exact** area of $△ABC$ shown above is{{field-1}} square units." 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290623 1072 #uuid "d1b7ea23-942e-5d6d-99bb-e09beee44db6" 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290623 1074 "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠B)=\\frac{5}{2}.$ Notice that relative to $∠B,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{AC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{BC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠B) & =\\frac{AC}{BC} \\\\ \\frac{5}{2} & =\\frac{3x-1}{12-5x} \\\\ 5(12-5x) & =2(3x-1) \\\\ 60-25x & =6x-2 \\\\ 31x & =62 \\\\ x & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =12-5x=12-5(2)=2, \\\\ AC & =3x-1=3(2)-1=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 5\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290624 1068 #edb/ref 17592186289965 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290624 1069 "q-251084" 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290624 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290624 1071 "![](images/45/4572bd2ef8f6086ed80f5ac21e045e3cf2359680872a958a40d2f1e72f22d980.png)\n\nGiven that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A)=2,$ the **exact** area of $△ABC$ shown above is{{field-1}} square units." 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290624 1072 #uuid "e4eb1820-1b1c-533a-934d-3a903e007b31" 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290624 1074 "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A)=2.$ Notice that relative to $∠A,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{AC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A) & =\\frac{BC}{AC} \\\\ 2 & =\\frac{9x+2}{5x-1} \\\\ 2(5x-1) & =9x+2 \\\\ 10x-2 & =9x+2 \\\\ x & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =9x+2=9(4)+2=38, \\\\ AC & =5x-1=5(4)-1=19.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 38\\cdot 19 \\\\  & =361.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290625 1068 #edb/ref 17592186290022 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290625 1069 "q-251086" 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290625 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290625 1071 "![](images/51/51e60c645aa6be034a8ef23d16a9ca7a815ca15fe815d7c3b03a866e693f3e5b.png)\n\nGiven that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A)=\\frac{2}{3},$ the **exact** area of $△ABC$ shown above is{{field-1}} square units." 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290625 1072 #uuid "bda5ec7b-0d2e-5231-8e0a-d3b2202c02ed" 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290625 1074 "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A)=\\frac{2}{3}.$ Notice that relative to $∠A,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{AC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A) & =\\frac{BC}{AC} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & =\\frac{10x-1}{8x+2} \\\\ 2(8x+2) & =3(10x-1) \\\\ 16x+4 & =30x-3 \\\\ 14x & =7 \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =10x-1=10(\\frac{1}{2})-1=4, \\\\ AC & =8x+2=8(\\frac{1}{2})+2=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290626 1068 #edb/ref 17592186289857 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290626 1069 "q-251087" 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290626 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290626 1071 "![](images/05/05003be9090f98f39a65d9ec33e8568fa43ec5c427e34398e4932708f8a03ccc.png)\n\nGiven that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A)=4,$ the **exact** area of $△ABC$ shown above is{{field-1}} square units." 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290626 1072 #uuid "fcc653a9-3324-58df-8a8e-f8dde641aa4c" 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290626 1074 "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A)=4.$ Notice that relative to $∠A,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{AC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A) & =\\frac{BC}{AC} \\\\ 4 & =\\frac{11x-12}{x+4} \\\\ 4(x+4) & =11x-12 \\\\ 4x+16 & =11x-12 \\\\ 7x & =28 \\\\ x & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =11x-12=11(4)-12=32, \\\\ AC & =x+4=4+4=8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 32\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =128.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290627 1068 #edb/ref 17592186290132 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290627 1069 "q-251088" 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290627 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290627 1071 "![](images/7e/7e555f1574ba37c5b2ac8f4bca54f0d9e2b449e1351f792feba334ddbdc5b8df.png)\n\nGiven that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠B)=\\sqrt{3},$ the **exact** area of $△ABC$ shown above is{{field-1}} square units." 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290627 1072 #uuid "67f70c4c-b54b-549e-9e7f-cfa7838f6c44" 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290627 1074 "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠B)=\\sqrt{3}.$ Notice that relative to $∠B,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{AC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{BC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠B) & =\\frac{AC}{BC} \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}(x-4)}{8-x} \\\\ \\sqrt{3}(8-x) & =\\sqrt{3}(x-4) \\\\ 8-x & =x-4 \\\\ 2x & =12 \\\\ x & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =8-x=8-6=2, \\\\ AC & =\\sqrt{3}(x-4)=\\sqrt{3}(6-4)=2\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\cdot 2\\sqrt{3} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290628 1068 #edb/ref 17592186290233 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290628 1069 "q-251089" 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290628 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290628 1071 "![](images/25/251ca3005dd302ec1e7ba0c7d7c497e28fd4c16cc0e431cc3691bdd4fe65446a.png)\n\nGiven that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠B)=\\frac{1}{5},$ the **exact** area of $△ABC$ shown above is{{field-1}} square units." 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290628 1072 #uuid "631e67df-da8d-5141-9930-394d0ee1d6b4" 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290628 1074 "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠B)=\\frac{1}{5}.$ Notice that relative to $∠B,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{AC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{BC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠B) & =\\frac{AC}{BC} \\\\ \\frac{1}{5} & =\\frac{6x-1}{15x} \\\\ 15x & =5(6x-1) \\\\ 15x & =30x-5 \\\\ 15x & =5 \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =15x=15(\\frac{1}{3})=5, \\\\ AC & =6x-1=6(\\frac{1}{3})-1=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 5\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290629 1068 #edb/ref 17592186290120 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290629 1069 "q-251111" 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290629 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290629 1071 "The coefficient of ${u}^{3}$ in the expansion of ${(1-u)}^{20}$ is{{field-1}}." 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290629 1072 #uuid "abe862de-c100-590b-b8f1-5a8ccac1a7dd" 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290629 1074 "The binomial expansion for $(1+x)^{n}$ is given by\n\n$$\n(1+x)^{n}=1+nx+\\frac{n(n-1)}{2!}{x}^{2}+⋯.\n$$\n\nIn particular, the ${x}^{3}$ term is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{n(n-1)(n-2)}{3!}{x}^{3}.\n$$\n\nReplacing $x$ with $-u$ and $n$ with $20$ in the above expression, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{20(20-1)(20-2)}{3!}\\cdot (-u)^{3} & =\\frac{20\\cdot 19\\cdot 18}{6}\\cdot (-u)^{3} \\\\  & =1140\\cdot (-{u}^{3}) \\\\  & =-1140{u}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coefficient of ${u}^{3}$ is $-1140.$" 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290630 1068 #edb/ref 17592186289936 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290630 1069 "q-251113" 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290630 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290630 1071 "The coefficient of ${m}^{4}$ in the expansion of ${(1-3m)}^{7}$ is{{field-1}}." 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290630 1072 #uuid "07e47311-22b9-594c-9372-90214018519e" 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290630 1074 "The binomial expansion for $(1+x)^{n}$ is given by\n\n$$\n(1+x)^{n}=1+nx+\\frac{n(n-1)}{2!}{x}^{2}+⋯.\n$$\n\nIn particular, the ${x}^{4}$ term is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{n(n-1)(n-2)(n-3)}{4!}{x}^{4}.\n$$\n\nReplacing $x$ with $-3m$ and $n$ with $7$ in the above expression, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7(7-1)(7-2)(7-3)}{4!}\\cdot (-3m)^{4} & =\\frac{7\\cdot 6\\cdot 5\\cdot 4}{24}\\cdot (-3)^{4}\\cdot {m}^{4} \\\\  & =35\\cdot 81{m}^{4} \\\\  & =2835{m}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coefficient of ${m}^{4}$ is $2835.$" 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290631 1068 #edb/ref 17592186289884 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290631 1069 "q-251116" 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290631 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290631 1071 "The coefficient of ${k}^{4}$ in the expansion of ${(1-\\frac{k}{4})}^{5}$ is{{field-1}}." 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290631 1072 #uuid "b9941abe-85c0-5263-b386-0b79bf9902cc" 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290631 1074 "The binomial expansion for $(1+x)^{n}$ is given by\n\n$$\n(1+x)^{n}=1+nx+\\frac{n(n-1)}{2!}{x}^{2}+⋯.\n$$\n\nIn particular, the ${x}^{4}$ term is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{n(n-1)(n-2)(n-3)}{4!}{x}^{4}.\n$$\n\nReplacing $x$ with $-\\frac{k}{4}$ and $n$ with $5$ in the above expression, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5(5-1)(5-2)(5-3)}{4!}\\cdot {(-\\frac{k}{4})}^{4} & =\\frac{5\\cdot 4\\cdot 3\\cdot 2}{24}\\cdot {(-\\frac{1}{4})}^{4}\\cdot {k}^{4} \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\frac{1}{256}{k}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{256}{k}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coefficient of ${k}^{4}$ is $\\frac{5}{256}.$" 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290632 1068 #edb/ref 17592186289816 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290632 1069 "q-251119" 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290632 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290632 1071 "The coefficient of ${u}^{4}$ in the expansion of ${(1+\\frac{2u}{3})}^{6}$ is{{field-1}}." 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290632 1072 #uuid "6a42edac-f50e-5d66-b9ec-a7c3b405c01e" 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290632 1074 "The binomial expansion for $(1+x)^{n}$ is given by\n\n$$\n(1+x)^{n}=1+nx+\\frac{n(n-1)}{2!}{x}^{2}+⋯.\n$$\n\nIn particular, the ${x}^{4}$ term is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{n(n-1)(n-2)(n-3)}{4!}{x}^{4}.\n$$\n\nReplacing $x$ with $\\frac{2u}{3}$ and $n$ with $6$ in the above expression, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6(6-1)(6-2)(6-3)}{4!}\\cdot {(\\frac{2u}{3})}^{4} & =\\frac{6\\cdot 5\\cdot 4\\cdot 3}{24}\\cdot {(\\frac{2}{3})}^{4}\\cdot {u}^{4} \\\\  & =15\\cdot \\frac{16}{81}{u}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{80}{27}{u}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coefficient of ${u}^{4}$ is $\\frac{80}{27}.$" 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290633 1068 #edb/ref 17592186289949 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290633 1069 "q-251121" 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290633 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290633 1071 "![](images/21/214774fb428c62ad5131760c2a073690bca63f6b8bb06131c4381fee943597c3.png)\n\nGiven that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =2,$ the **exact** area of $△ABC$ shown above is{{field-1}} square units." 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290633 1072 #uuid "9915aa64-9757-581e-b221-8c1fd3dfbe6d" 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290633 1074 "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =2,$ where $\\theta =m∠A.$ Notice we're also given the length of the side $\\overset{―}{AC}$ adjacent to $∠A.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to find the length of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{BC}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{BC}{AC} \\\\ 2 & =\\frac{BC}{15} \\\\ BC & =2\\cdot 15 \\\\ BC & =30\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 30\\cdot 15 \\\\  & =225.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290634 1068 #edb/ref 17592186289890 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290634 1069 "q-251125" 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290634 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290634 1071 "![](images/58/58af9726d81e1d926f814736fa92dc95c427d4346c40252470380f51a5fcf50a.png)\n\nGiven that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =3,$ the **exact** area of $△ABC$ shown above is{{field-1}} square units." 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290634 1072 #uuid "5b27069b-1b32-57bd-8872-02874835d53f" 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290634 1074 "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =3,$ where $\\theta =m∠B.$ Notice we're also given the length of the side $\\overset{―}{AC}$ opposite to $∠B.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to find the length of the adjacent side $\\overset{―}{BC}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{AC}{BC} \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{15}{BC} \\\\ BC & =\\frac{15}{3} \\\\ BC & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 15\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =37.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290635 1068 #edb/ref 17592186289807 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290635 1069 "q-251126" 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290635 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290635 1071 "![](images/ef/ef2b0447e81370a50ea6d4115fc6f4687aff74fee17bc66f116b3c732667857e.png)\n\nGiven that $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{2}{7},$ the **exact** area of $△ABC$ shown above is{{field-1}} square units." 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290635 1072 #uuid "9ff5d5b6-163a-5609-884c-9ac6ae774a4f" 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290635 1074 "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{2}{7},$ where $\\theta =m∠B.$ Notice we're also given the length of the side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ adjacent to $∠B.$ Hence, we can use the cosine ratio to find the length of the hypotenuse $\\overset{―}{AB}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{BC}{AB} \\\\ \\frac{2}{7} & =\\frac{4}{AB} \\\\ AB & =\\frac{4}{2}\\cdot 7 \\\\ AB & =14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can use the Pythagorean Theorem to find the missing side $AC:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =\\sqrt{A{B}^{2}-B{C}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{14}^{2}-{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{196-16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{180} \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 6\\sqrt{5}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =12\\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290636 1068 #edb/ref 17592186290259 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290636 1069 "q-251127" 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290636 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290636 1071 "![](images/ba/ba89c2cf139dd6251804ed0758c4edc4690463ba5ae14867549881a29736f9e6.png)\n\nGiven that $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{12}{13},$ the **exact** area of $△ABC$ shown above is{{field-1}} square units." 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290636 1072 #uuid "56140f3b-db4f-5312-8154-161eb9c11c33" 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290636 1074 "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{12}{13},$ where $\\theta =m∠B.$ Notice we're also given the length of the side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ adjacent to $∠B.$ Hence, we can use the cosine ratio to find the length of the hypotenuse $\\overset{―}{AB}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{BC}{AB} \\\\ \\frac{12}{13} & =\\frac{12}{AB} \\\\ AB & =\\frac{12}{12}\\cdot 13 \\\\ AB & =13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can use the Pythagorean Theorem to find the missing side $AC:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =\\sqrt{A{B}^{2}-B{C}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{13}^{2}-{12}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{169-144} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 5\\cdot 12 \\\\  & =30.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290637 1068 #edb/ref 17592186290034 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290637 1069 "q-251130" 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290637 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290637 1071 "![](images/6b/6b1c6c90b25fa7c4cd4cde42bdcd5e69a2ccef63f1945067a8f62dc7ee779f05.png)\n\nGiven that $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{7},$ the **exact** area of $△ABC$ shown above is{{field-1}} square units." 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290637 1072 #uuid "041ce151-ea34-5d92-9b45-b61b0961f5d4" 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290637 1074 "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{7},$ where $\\theta =m∠A.$ Notice we're also given the length of the side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ opposite to $∠A.$ Hence, we can use the sine ratio to find the length of the hypotenuse $\\overset{―}{AB}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{BC}{AB} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{7} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{AB} \\\\ AB & =\\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{\\sqrt{13}}\\cdot 7 \\\\ AB & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can use the Pythagorean Theorem to find the missing side $AC:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =\\sqrt{A{B}^{2}-B{C}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{7}^{2}-(\\sqrt{13})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{49-13} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36} \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{13}\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290638 1068 #edb/ref 17592186289860 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290638 1069 "q-251187" 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290638 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290638 1071 "![](images/d7/d792a93992bbd915063156e0c8fb4f65a71f1609cee5141609e4a5ca6ba6f405.png)\n\nThe **exact** area of $△ABC$ shown above is{{field-1}} square units." 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290638 1072 #uuid "f74b12e2-81b7-5343-90f1-6de4ef965311" 13194139533408 17592186045585 true] [17592186290638 1074 "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AB\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $m∠C={30}^{∘}.$ Notice that relative to $∠C,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{AB}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{BC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠C) & =\\frac{AB}{BC} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡({30}^{∘}) & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}(x-1)}{2x+1} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}(x-1)}{2x+1} \\\\ \\sqrt{3}(2x+1) & =3\\sqrt{3}(x-1) \\\\ 2x+1 & =3x-3 \\\\ x & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\sqrt{3}(x-1)=\\sqrt{3}(4-1)=3\\sqrt{3}, \\\\ BC & =2x+1=2(4)+1=9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot AB\\cdot BC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 3\\sqrt{3}\\cdot 9 \\\\  & =\\frac{27\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533408 17592186045585 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-000ea0dc-e83d-59b3-891d-03ba54bde6ba" 17592186288031 "answer-0043b9dd-acd7-5722-ae3f-3f717ea8f717" 17592186288032 "answer-0083447b-7bf3-52b5-bfed-3ab32b17af3c" 17592186288033 "answer-00837155-5f27-503a-a52f-c2a043e66010" 17592186288034 "answer-00acbd21-382b-5ab9-ae57-615f612cac26" 17592186288035 "answer-00e0441d-7176-5665-92dd-c26fbcb98df8" 17592186288036 "answer-015883a9-a728-56a9-911a-2c70c5c410e8" 17592186288037 "answer-016d8eac-f654-53ff-87e9-866f859b2632" 17592186288038 "answer-017b399a-6ce5-5ff1-ab6d-1342fd54f7a5" 